        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(control-ui): multi-pane split view for chat",
        "body": "Fixes #100690\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Control UI chat page renders exactly one session at a time. Operators running several agent sessions in parallel have to bounce through the sidebar or open extra browser tabs, and cannot watch one agent run while prompting another.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a proper split screen mode to the chat page with arbitrarily many panes (Claude Desktop-style tiling: columns side by side, each column a vertical stack). Implemented as a real refactor rather than a bolt-on:\n\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/split-layout.ts` — pure, immutable layout model (create / split right / split down / close with column collapse / pair-local resize with 15% clamps / normalize-on-load with id+weight repair). Fully unit-tested, no DOM.\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-pane.ts` — the session-scoped chat machinery extracted out of `ChatPage` into `openclaw-chat-pane` (state controller, gateway/config/sessions subscriptions, composer persistence, run lifecycle). Each pane is a full chat: own session, transcript, composer, tool stream.\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-page.ts` — now a thin layout host: renders the pane grid with keyed `repeat`, owns the route ↔ active pane sync, layout persistence, and dividers.\n- Exactly one pane is **active** and owns global chrome (URL, sidebar selection, command palette target, `gateway.setSessionKey`, persisted `sessionKey`/`lastActiveSessionKey`). Clicking or focusing a pane activates it; guards on both sync directions prevent navigation loops. `resetChatStateForRouteSession` no longer writes global session settings — that write now belongs exclusively to the active pane's bindings.\n- Per-pane presentation state: the module-singleton composer state (slash menu) and thread state (search, history render window) are keyed by pane id; DOM ids that would duplicate across panes (settings popover, slash listbox/options) are pane-scoped.\n- `resizable-divider` gains a `horizontal` orientation (stacked panes): Y-axis drag, Up/Down keys, `aria-orientation`, and pair-local measurement so a drag among N siblings only redistributes the two adjacent panes.\n- Layout persists as a browser-local Control UI preference (`chatSplitLayout` in `UiSettings`), validated by `normalizeChatSplitLayout` on load; the key is omitted from storage when split view is closed. No URL surface, no gateway/protocol changes, no routing changes.\n- Narrow viewports render only the active pane (layout preserved); its pane header keeps session switching and close, while split buttons are hidden so panes can't be created invisibly.\n\nKnown tradeoff: entering/leaving split mode recreates the pane elements (different template shape), so transcripts reload once from the gateway on those transitions.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can supervise any number of agent sessions in one browser window: split any pane right or down, give each pane its own session via the pane header, resize with draggable/keyboard-accessible dividers, and get the same layout back after a reload. The classic single-pane chat is unchanged when split view is off.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused suites (133 tests, all green): `pnpm test ui/src/pages/chat/split-layout.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-page.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/app/settings.node.test.ts ui/src/components/resizable-divider.test.ts` → `Test Files 5 passed (5) / Tests 133 passed (133)`.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` regenerated bundles; `pnpm ui:i18n:check` clean, 0 fallbacks across all 20 locales.\n- Deterministic mock-gateway visual proof (Playwright against `startControlUiE2eServer` + `installMockGateway`):\n\n| Classic (unchanged) | Two columns |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![classic](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/split-view-100690/01-classic.png) | ![two columns](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/split-view-100690/02-two-columns.png) |\n\n| Three panes, per-pane sessions | Resized divider | Layout after reload |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ![three panes](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/split-view-100690/03-three-panes.png) | ![resized](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/split-view-100690/04-resized.png) | ![after reload](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/split-view-100690/05-after-reload.png) |\n\nThe three-pane shot also proves the active pane drives the sidebar/URL (sidebar highlights the split pane's session after switching it) and the reload shot proves layout + divider sizes persist.\n",
        "branch": "claude/dazzling-hermann-ba116c",
